description.narrative:
Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government (i) completed a TADAT Assessmentf to measure the extent to which good tax administration practices are in place in DGT, (ii) issued regulations that outline duties and professional standards for specific categories of tax officers, and (iii) designed and implemented a comprehensive learning curriculum to train tax officials on how to use Coretax ahead of its operationalization

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government (i) operationalized a Compliance Committee at DGT, to develop and systematically manage implementation of compliance improvement plans that mitigate taxpayer compliance risks, and (ii) adopted end-to-end business processes for supervising taxpayer compliance that improve efficiency and accountability in risk management

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government (i) replaced Tax Identification Numbers of individual taxpayers with the National ID numbers, ensuring that taxpayer data can be more easily cross-checked against third-party sources, be disaggregated according to sex, and providing greater access and inclusivity opportunities to women taxpayers, (ii) issued regulations outlining standardized procedures to maintain the reliability and quality of the taxpayer database, and (iii) operationalized Coretax to streamline DGT business processes, improve DGT business intelligence, and reduce taxpayer compliance costs.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government (i) rolled-out a women-to-women coaching program in DGT to better prepare women tax officials for leadership positions, and (ii) issued regulations on the reporting and investigation of violations by MOF officials (including harassment, and disregard of the code of ethics and conduct), and the provision of whistleblower protection

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government issued regulations to streamline refund process for VAT overpayment by MSMEs including provisions that raise the threshold for preliminary VAT refunds not subject to prior audit by DGT from Rp1 billion to Rp5 billion.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will (i) complete the migration of remaining legacy systems to accommodate regulatory/business process changes into Coretax, and (ii) implement a taxpayer education campaign to empower taxpayers to make full use of Coretax, including targeted interventions for women taxpayers and women business associations.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will (i) establish a dedicated filing enforcement operations team, with full-time staff trained in customer relations and negotiation techniques, and (ii) operationalize the monitoring and evaluation process for tax audits.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will (i) further enhance Coretax based on a comprehensive review of system functionality, including towards women and for marginalized groups, and (ii) collect, analyze, and disseminate taxpayer data, including sex-disaggregated data, for policymaking.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will (i) operationalize a framework to systematically monitor and evaluate compliance risk mitigation activities using CRM; (ii) implement a risk-based and centralized case selection system for tax audits using CRM, and (iii) merge DGT&apos;s existing Compliance Risk Management Information System with Coretax to improve the scope for intelligence gathering and research on compliance risk.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will further enhance DGT&apos;s HR system to promote staff safety and wellbeing in accordance with DGT&apos;s medium-term modernization plan

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will implement measures to expand the use of the fast-track refund system, including adoption of the automated risk assessment for inclusion in the fast-track scheme.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will issue regulations to streamline and enhance the tax dispute resolution function, including a measure to expedite processes though Coretax.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will undertake a comprehensive review of taxpayer dispute resolution in Indonesia, and will implement measures to address identified issues.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will undertake a comprehensive review of the VAT refund process, and will implement measures to address identified issues.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will upgrade DGT&apos;s human resource management information system (HRMIS) and integrate it with Coretax, allowing for better performance measurement of the organization&apos;s human resources.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will: (i) adopt and begin implementation of a new medium-term modernization plan for DGT, which contains explicit actions and targets to mainstream gender in tax administration, and (ii) issue gender-responsive regulations on DGT staff rotation to field offices, which provide additional flexibility to married couples and families with special needs children, while allowing them to maintain career advancement.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government will: (i) implement a new operating model for the tax administration to reflect the increased digitalization of business processes, and to structure the organization on functional lines; (ii) enhance the knowledge management system for staff to ensure they are properly educated on new ways of working, and (iii) operationalize structured processes for the identification, analysis, and evaluation of operational and human resource risks in DGT.

Reform area: Enhanced efficiency and effectiveness of domestic tax administration 

Outcome: At least 75 million valid taxpayers registered in Coretax. ; 

Description: The government, through MOF, restructured the Directorate of Tax Objection and Appeals and decentralized the handling disputes, appeals and lawsuits to Regional Tax offices in Jakarta to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of DGT in taxpayer dispute resolution.
